# S12.1 final review: nested Git metadata symlinks

## Finding

The root Git layout guard rejected a symlinked top-level object directory,
`commondir` and object alternates, but did not reject a nested symlink such as
`.git/refs/heads` or `.git/logs/refs/heads`. Root Git could consequently follow
that link outside the quarantined Git directory.

## Resolution

Before any root Git operation, the complete Git metadata tree is now scanned
with `lstat` semantics. Every entry must be a direct directory or regular file;
all symlinks and special files are rejected. Regression coverage reproduces
both nested reference and nested reflog symlinks.
